{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00298",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.78,
      "end_seconds": 6.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I brought my bag, is it fine to leave it here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.97,
      "end_seconds": 12.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Yes, come in, take a seat. What can I do for you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.6,
      "end_seconds": 18.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "It's a throbbing headache on one side. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.55,
      "end_seconds": 23.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.22,
      "end_seconds": 29.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "About a seven out of ten. It's worse with loud noise and bright lights."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.75,
      "end_seconds": 36.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.47,
      "end_seconds": 46.04,
      "duration_seconds": 8.57,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get sensitivity to light as well. The sensitivity to light? That's been for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.41,
      "end_seconds": 49.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.35,
      "end_seconds": 55.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say. Oh, and vomiting. That's been about the same, three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.74,
      "end_seconds": 70.23,
      "duration_seconds": 13.49,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.83,
      "end_seconds": 74.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Right, thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.43,
      "end_seconds": 81.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any fever, loss of consciousness or weakness in the arms or legs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.36,
      "end_seconds": 90.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "Um, I haven't had fever, loss of consciousness or weakness in the arms or legs, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.51,
      "end_seconds": 106.43,
      "duration_seconds": 12.92,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.99,
      "end_seconds": 109.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.05,
      "end_seconds": 113.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.53,
      "end_seconds": 118.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "I'm allergic to sulfa drugs, I get a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.81,
      "end_seconds": 122.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.0,
      "end_seconds": 123.82,
      "duration_seconds": 0.82,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.23,
      "end_seconds": 141.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Let's go through your medication. What are you taking? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.83,
      "end_seconds": 145.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "I'm on escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.07,
      "end_seconds": 149.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.4,
      "end_seconds": 153.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Right, yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.9,
      "end_seconds": 160.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.55,
      "end_seconds": 162.54,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Yes, anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.92,
      "end_seconds": 169.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "I see. So, is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.79,
      "end_seconds": 174.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.26,
      "end_seconds": 177.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.51,
      "end_seconds": 179.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "No operations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.94,
      "end_seconds": 193.67,
      "duration_seconds": 12.73,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.28,
      "end_seconds": 197.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.94,
      "end_seconds": 202.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.44,
      "end_seconds": 215.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.05,
      "end_seconds": 236.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.4 degrees, respiratory rate 16, heart rate 78, pressure 126 over 76."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.32,
      "end_seconds": 239.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.56,
      "end_seconds": 244.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment. Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.65,
      "end_seconds": 261.17,
      "duration_seconds": 15.52,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.83,
      "end_seconds": 265.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Alright, I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.56,
      "end_seconds": 268.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.97,
      "end_seconds": 276.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "So, based on your history, I think we're dealing with a migraine pattern at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.22,
      "end_seconds": 279.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.63,
      "end_seconds": 296.09,
      "duration_seconds": 16.46,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a migraine pattern is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a throbbing headache on one side, and no fever or weakness in the arms or legs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.5,
      "end_seconds": 298.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.26,
      "end_seconds": 303.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.32,
      "end_seconds": 305.02,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.52,
      "end_seconds": 320.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.57,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. We should do an MRI of the brain for recurrent headaches. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.12,
      "end_seconds": 323.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.62,
      "end_seconds": 330.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "I'd like you to take domperidone, 10 milligrams, when nauseous, as needed. It's for migraine nausea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.13,
      "end_seconds": 333.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.7,
      "end_seconds": 347.52,
      "duration_seconds": 12.82,
      "text": "I'm prescribing propranolol, 20 milligrams, twice a day, for three months. You take it by mouth. That should help with migraine prevention. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.88,
      "end_seconds": 349.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.56,
      "end_seconds": 359.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Keep a headache diary, things like skipped meals, poor sleep, certain foods and the weather."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.09,
      "end_seconds": 386.88,
      "duration_seconds": 26.79,
      "text": "Go on. Try not to skip meals and keep your sleep regular. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. If you have the worst headache of your life or any weakness, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.45,
      "end_seconds": 388.15,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.54,
      "end_seconds": 390.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Let's review you in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 393.29,
      "end_seconds": 396.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 397.46,
      "end_seconds": 402.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.42,
      "end_seconds": 413.2,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "So, I take the domperidone, 10 milligrams, when nauseous and take the propranolol, 20 milligrams, twice a day. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.66,
      "end_seconds": 418.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Okay, yes, exactly right. Okay, I think we're finished. Is everything clear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.88,
      "end_seconds": 423.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "That's everything I wanted to ask. Thank you."
    }
  ]
}